The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/control-deep/ctrldp-03-priority-tier-assignment.md`.

**Summary of findings:**

- **6 findings total**: 2 critical, 2 high, 2 medium
- **Critical**: No centralized signal-to-tier mapping (Finding 1) — tier assignment is scattered across actors with no compiler-enforced coverage. Safety tier exists but is never used by any built-in actor (Finding 2) — freeze/overheat/emergency protection has no dispatch pathway.
- **High**: Same-tier conflict resolution is undocumented last-write-wins, making multi-actor scenarios dependent on registration order (Finding 3). DR TurnOff at Grid tier can override everything with no thermal safety backstop (Finding 6).
- **Medium**: Cross-pass priority inversion is correctly prevented but uses linear search (Finding 4). Tier system extensibility has no compile-time guards and the `PRIORITY_TIER_COUNT` const + `#[repr(u8)]` discriminants can drift from the derived `Ord` (Finding 5).
